# Multi-agent file locks

This repo may be edited by **Cursor** and **Claude Desktop** (or other agents) in the same directory.

## Hard rule

Before creating or editing a file with Write/StrReplace (or equivalent), acquire an advisory lock:

```bash
UAETRAIL_AGENT_ID=claude node .cursor/hooks/agent-file-lock.mjs acquire <path>
```

Cursor Auto acquires locks via `.cursor/hooks.json` (`UAETRAIL_AGENT_ID` defaults to `cursor`).

If acquire fails because another agent holds the lock: **do not overwrite** — pick another file, wait, or tell the user.

Release when done with that file:

```bash
UAETRAIL_AGENT_ID=claude node .cursor/hooks/agent-file-lock.mjs release <path>
```

Or release all of yours at session end:

```bash
UAETRAIL_AGENT_ID=claude node .cursor/hooks/agent-file-lock.mjs release-mine
```

## Safer than locks

Prefer **separate git worktrees/branches** for parallel agents. Locks are advisory and only work if every agent uses them.
